---
/**
 * Applies the reader's saved theme before anything paints. The toggle that
 * saves it is in SiteNav.astro; this is the half that has to run first.
 *
 * Every page's <html> is written with `data-theme="dark"` — dark is the
 * default, and a reader who never touches the toggle gets it whatever their
 * OS says. A stored choice overrides that attribute here.
 *
 * Three things make it work on a static site:
 *
 * - `is:inline` keeps Astro from bundling it, so it stays a plain blocking
 *   script rather than a module that defers.
 * - It must sit in <head>, before any markup paints. A script that ran after
 *   the body would show a flash of the default theme first.
 * - `<ClientRouter />` copies the incoming page's <html> attributes over on
 *   every soft navigation, which would put `data-theme="dark"` back, so the
 *   choice is re-applied on `astro:after-swap`. The listener is bound once:
 *   the router may re-run this script.
 *
 * localStorage can throw (blocked site data, some private windows), so every
 * read is guarded and a failure just leaves the default.
 */
---

<script is:inline>
	(() => {
		const apply = () => {
			let theme = null;
			try {
				theme = localStorage.getItem('theme');
			} catch {}
			if (theme === 'light' || theme === 'dark') document.documentElement.dataset.theme = theme;
		};

		apply();
		if (window.__themeSwapBound) return;
		window.__themeSwapBound = true;
		document.addEventListener('astro:after-swap', apply);
	})();
</script>
